{
  "conversation_lines": [
    {
      "turn_number": 1,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, I'm Dr. Lee. I’ll be taking care of you during this hospital stay. Can you tell me what brought you in today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 2,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Hi, Doctor. I’ve been vomiting since 5 a.m. I haven’t eaten anything, and it’s just watery. I also have a headache and felt chills earlier."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 3,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I see. You’ve had episodes like this before, right? Does this feel similar?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 4,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, exactly like before. It’s the same pattern—nausea, then vomiting, and I just can’t keep anything down."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 5,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Okay. The nurses mentioned you sometimes make yourself vomit because it helps you feel better. Is that true?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 6,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yeah… when I drink water or ginger ale, I feel worse unless I bring it up. It gives me some relief, even if it’s not normal."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 7,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:36:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "I understand. But repeatedly inducing vomiting can cause serious problems—like electrolyte imbalances, damage to your esophagus, or even heart issues."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 8,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:37:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I didn’t realize it was that dangerous. I just do it because it feels like the only thing that helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 9,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:38:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll work on safer ways to manage that urge. For now, we’re going to keep you on IV fluids and give you medications to help with nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 10,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:39:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, that sounds good. My blood sugar’s probably high too, since I haven’t eaten but I’m still vomiting."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 11,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:40:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, your glucose was 395 when you arrived. We’ve given you insulin and fluids to help correct that. We’ll keep monitoring it closely."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 12,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:41:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you. My blood pressure’s always high during these episodes too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 13,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:42:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s 158/86 now, and your heart rate is elevated. That’s likely from the stress, vomiting, and maybe not absorbing your blood pressure meds because you’re vomiting them."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 14,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:43:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Makes sense. I take metoprolol and lisinopril at home."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 15,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:44:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’ll restart those once you can keep oral meds down. For now, we may need to give you IV blood pressure medication if it stays high."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 16,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:45:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’ve been doing this for years—doctors always say it’s my diabetes or gastroparesis."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 17,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:46:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You do have type 1 diabetes and a history of gastroparesis, but your recent gastric motility study was normal. That makes us think this might not be purely a stomach-emptying issue."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 18,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:47:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So what is it then?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 19,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:48:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re considering that anxiety or a functional disorder might be playing a big role. The fact that you feel better after inducing vomiting suggests a behavioral component."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 20,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:49:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I do get really anxious during these episodes. But it’s hard to tell what comes first—the nausea or the anxiety."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 21,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:50:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Exactly. They can feed into each other. We’re going to start you on Ativan for anxiety, which may also help with nausea."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 22,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:51:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ve never taken that before. Is it safe?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 23,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:52:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, it’s commonly used for anxiety and nausea. We’ll start low and only use it as needed. We’re also increasing your citalopram dose to 20 mg daily to help with mood and anxiety long-term."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 24,
      "time": "2199-03-15 14:53:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, I trust you. I just want to feel better."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 25,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:15:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. How are you feeling today?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 26,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:16:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "A little better. I haven’t vomited since last night, and I didn’t make myself do it either."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 27,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:17:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s great progress. Your labs are improving—your white count was high yesterday at 12.3, but it’s down to 9.8 this morning."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 28,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:18:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Is that infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 29,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:19:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Not necessarily. High white counts can happen with stress, vomiting, or dehydration. It’s coming down now that you’re more stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 30,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:20:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Oh, good. My throat’s been a little sore too."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 31,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:21:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re planning an EGD tomorrow to look into your stomach. We may do another botox injection, which has helped you before."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 32,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:22:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Yes, I want to do that. It helped last time."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 33,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:23:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Also, we’ll take biopsies during the EGD to check for inflammation or infection, especially since your throat is sore."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 34,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:24:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Could it be an infection?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 35,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:25:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Possibly. Sometimes people with diabetes get esophageal candidiasis. We’ll start fluconazole just in case, even before the biopsy results."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 36,
      "time": "2199-03-16 09:26:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay, thanks. I’ll take it as prescribed."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 37,
      "time": "2199-03-17 13:30:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Hi, you’re back from your EGD. The procedure went well. You received botox in the stomach, which may help reduce vomiting episodes."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 38,
      "time": "2199-03-17 13:31:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s good. Did they see anything unusual?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 39,
      "time": "2199-03-17 13:32:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The endoscopist saw areas that looked like candidiasis, so biopsies were taken. But preliminary report says no fungal infection was found."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 40,
      "time": "2199-03-17 13:33:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "So why do I have a sore throat?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 41,
      "time": "2199-03-17 13:34:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "The biopsy did show inflammation and an ulcer, but no fungus or virus. We’ll keep you on fluconazole for now and discuss with your PCP whether to continue after discharge."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 42,
      "time": "2199-03-17 13:35:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Okay. I’m glad the botox was done. I hope it helps."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 43,
      "time": "2199-03-18 10:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re doing well. You’ve kept down clear liquids and now a soft diet. Your blood pressure is also much better—150/70 today."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 44,
      "time": "2199-03-18 10:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel stronger. I haven’t had the urge to vomit, even when I drink water."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 45,
      "time": "2199-03-18 10:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s excellent. We’re going to advance you to a regular diet today. We’re also restarting your regular meds by mouth."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 46,
      "time": "2199-03-18 10:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Great. What about the Ativan and fluconazole?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 47,
      "time": "2199-03-18 10:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ll take Ativan as needed for anxiety or nausea for the next four days. Fluconazole for four days total—then talk to your PCP about continuing."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 48,
      "time": "2199-03-19 11:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’ve had no vomiting for two days, your labs are stable, and you’re eating well. We’re planning to discharge you tomorrow."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 49,
      "time": "2199-03-19 11:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "That’s great news. Should I see my psychiatrist?"
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 50,
      "time": "2199-03-19 11:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, we strongly recommend psychiatric follow-up. We’re giving you a letter with resources for counseling and relaxation techniques."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 51,
      "time": "2199-03-19 11:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I’ll make the appointment. I want to stop this cycle."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 52,
      "time": "2199-03-19 11:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "That’s the right step. Also, please don’t induce vomiting—it can lead to serious complications like heart rhythm issues or esophageal tears."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 53,
      "time": "2199-03-19 11:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I promise I’ll try. Thank you for helping me."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 54,
      "time": "2199-03-20 08:00:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Good morning. You’re cleared for discharge. You’re alert, eating well, and your vitals are stable."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 55,
      "time": "2199-03-20 08:01:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "I feel so much better than when I came in."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 56,
      "time": "2199-03-20 08:02:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "We’re sending you home with updated meds: citalopram 20 mg daily, Ativan as needed, and fluconazole for four days. Continue your regular diabetes and blood pressure meds."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 57,
      "time": "2199-03-20 08:03:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Got it. And I’ll follow up with GI and my PCP."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 58,
      "time": "2199-03-20 08:04:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "Yes, and please schedule psychiatric follow-up. We’re here if anything changes, but we expect you’ll continue improving."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 59,
      "time": "2199-03-20 08:05:00",
      "speaker": "Patient",
      "text": "Thank you, Doctor. I really appreciate your care."
    },
    {
      "turn_number": 60,
      "time": "2199-03-20 08:06:00",
      "speaker": "Doctor",
      "text": "You’re welcome. Take care, and we’ll see you in follow-up if needed."
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "admission_start": "2199-03-15 14:26:00",
    "admission_end": "2199-03-20 15:09:00",
    "summary_paragraph": "A woman with type 1 diabetes and a history of recurrent vomiting was admitted for intractable nausea and vomiting, similar to prior episodes. She was observed self-inducing vomiting, which raised concern for a functional or anxiety-related component rather than pure gastroparesis, especially given a recent normal gastric motility study. She received IV fluids, antiemetics, and Ativan for anxiety, with improvement. An EGD with botox injection was performed, and esophageal biopsies showed ulceration but no fungal infection despite clinical suspicion of candidiasis; fluconazole was continued pending PCP follow-up. Her blood pressure, initially elevated due to vomiting and anxiety, stabilized with IV and oral medications. She gradually advanced to a regular diet, remained asymptomatic, and was discharged home with psychiatric referral, updated medications including increased citalopram and short-term Ativan, and instructions to avoid self-induced vomiting.",
    "problems": [
      "Persistent vomiting",
      "Candidal esophagitis",
      "Diabetes with neurological manifestations, type I [juvenile type], uncontrolled",
      "Gastroparesis",
      "Polyneuropathy in diabetes",
      "Unspecified essential hypertension",
      "Anxiety state, unspecified"
    ]
  }
}
